solution.p:
                                                                        Because \triangle{}OBA\sim{}\triangle{}ODC, we know that \frac{OA}{OB}=\frac{OC}{OD}, so substituting the known lengths, we have

\frac{OC}{OD}=\frac{OA}{OB}&\rightarrow\frac{OC}{3\text{m}}=\frac{0.5\text{m}}{1\text{m}}
&\rightarrow{OC}={3\text{m}}\frac{0.5\text{m}}{1\text{m}}
&\rightarrow{OC}={1.5\text{m}}

 From the Pythagorean theorem, since \triangle{}BAO is a right triangle, we have \left(BA\right)^{2}+\left(OA\right)^{2}=\left(OB\right)^{2}, so \left(BA\right)^{2}+\left(0.5\right)^{2}=\left(1\right)^2, so

        \left(BA\right)^{2}&=\left(1\right)^2-\left(0.5\right)^{2}
                           &=1-0.25
                           &=0.75
                           &=\frac{3}{4} 

so

        BA&=\sqrt{\frac{3}{4}}
          &=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{4}}
          &=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{{2}}
          &\approx 0.866025.

