statement.p:
Multiplying both sides by \sin(0.69474), we have

        d&=\frac{30\text{m}\sin(0.69474)}{\cos(0.69474)}
        &\approx 25\text{m}

image.latex-image:
\begin{tikzpicture}
% Observer
\coordinate (O) at (-2,0);
\node[above left] at (O) {Inaya};
\fill (O) circle (0.05);
% Tree Base
\coordinate (T0) at (0,0);
% Tree Top
\coordinate (T1) at (0,4.5);
% Tick marks for Observer and Tree Base
\draw
($(O)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(O)-(0,0.3)$)
($(T0)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(T0)-(0,0.3)$)
;
% Ground
\draw[thick]
        ($(O)+(-1,0)$) -- ($(T0)+(1,0)$);
;
% Distance Arrow Between Observer and Base
\draw[stealth-stealth]
($(O)-(0,0.2)$) -- node[midway,below] {\(10\)m} ($(T0)-(0,0.2)$)
;
\draw[dotted,thick]
% Observer to tree top
        (O) -- (T1)
% base to tree top, labeled \(d\) midway
        -- node[midway,right] {\(d\)} (T0);
% Angle indicator
\draw[-stealth]
let
\p1 =  (O),
\p2 = (T0),
\p3 = (T1),
\n1 = {atan((\y3-\y2)/(\x2-\x1))},
\n2 = {\n1*3.14159/(180pt)},
in
($(\p1)+(0.5,0)$)
arc[
        start angle=0,
        end angle=\n1,
        radius=0.5
]
node[midway,right] {\scriptsize\(\theta\approx \pgfmathparse{\n2}\pgfmathresult\) rad}
;
\end{tikzpicture}

solution.p:
We know the coordinates of the point on the unit circle are (\cos(\theta),\sin(theta)), and we know that the sides of the small triangle are proportional to the sides of the big triangle. Thus, \frac{d}{10\text{m}}=\frac{\sin(\theta)}{\cos(\theta)}, so we have

        d&=10\text{m}\frac{\sin(\theta)}{\cos(\theta)}
         &=10\text{m}\frac{\sin(1.15251)}{\cos(1.15251)}
         &=22.5\text{m}

